The issue seems to be Flutter not properly setting screen geometry after the virtual keyboard is dismissed (web on Android). I have a partially working workaround that detects the issue reliably and attempts to re-invoke and clear the virtual keyboard so that the screen bounds reset. HOWEVER: this code needs some type of debouncing in it b/c while it works on the emulator, on a real device it is causing the virtual keyboard to go nuts.

```
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter/services.dart';
import 'package:logging/logging.dart';

final _log = Logger('ViewInsetObserver');

// See: https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues/124205
class ViewInsetObserver extends WidgetsBindingObserver {
  double _lastViewInsetBottom = 0;

  @override
  void didChangeMetrics() {
    final view = WidgetsBinding.instance.platformDispatcher.views.first;
    final viewInsets = view.viewInsets;
    final viewInsetBottom = viewInsets.bottom;

    // Check if view inset bottom became negative
    if (viewInsetBottom < 0 && _lastViewInsetBottom >= 0) {
      _log.warning('Negative view inset detected: $viewInsetBottom');

      _refocusAndDismiss();
    }

    _lastViewInsetBottom = viewInsetBottom;
  }

  // NOTE: This needs some type of debouncing or delay to work properly
  void _refocusAndDismiss() {
    final focusNode = FocusManager.instance.primaryFocus;
    if (focusNode == null) {
      _log.info('No focus node found -- need a different workaround?');
      return;
    }
    _log.warning('Unfocusing node: $focusNode');
    // This is super dirty!
    // We need to defocus, and then re-request focus after a short delay
    // and then defocus again so that the keyboard goes away naturally
    focusNode.unfocus();
    const delay = Duration(milliseconds: 50);
    Future.delayed(
      delay,
      focusNode.requestFocus,
    ).then((_) => Future.delayed(delay, focusNode.unfocus));
  }
}
```

You can add it to your main so that it detects across all screens:

```
  WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
  WidgetsBinding.instance.addObserver(ViewInsetObserver());
```
